<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="c2c5a788">&lt;p&gt;
    Meet with the stakeholders to understand their needs and current environment as well as discuss potential future state
    options that may address those needs. It is quite common to have various groups of stakeholders&amp;nbsp;with conflicting
    needs.&amp;nbsp;So, it is necessary to analyze and triangulate (estimate) all of them in order to create a consistent and
    compelling vision of the product for the stakeholders. It is then possible to discuss and agree upon a single vision of
    what the final product or service will encompass with the stakeholders.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Once a vision has been agreed upon,&amp;nbsp;use it to assist with the initial outlining of a specific set of deliverables
    that will help achieve that vision, potentially iteratively and incrementally. This may also be used to facilitate the
    initial planning and development activities. This process may take several iterations while working with the
    stakeholders to reach a final vision. Ultimately, it is important to agree upon the vision with the stakeholders as one
    of the first steps for any project as it guides other more detailed activities.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
